guide='<!doctype html><html><head><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><title>Eye Trace ABS fit tests</title><style>body{font:16px system-ui;max-width:1050px;margin:30px auto;padding:20px;color:#182d40}img{max-width:100%;max-height:460px;object-fit:contain;display:block;margin:auto}section{border-top:1px solid #aaa;margin:28px 0;padding-top:18px}li{margin:8px 0}.hold{background:#fff0cd;padding:15px}</style></head><body><h1>Eye Trace - ABS physical fit tests</h1><p class=\"hold\"><b>Print first:</b> <a href=\"STL/EyeTrace_ABS_FitTests_SevenCoupons_FINAL.stl\">EyeTrace_ABS_FitTests_SevenCoupons_FINAL.stl</a> (seven coupons, supports off). Physical tests NOT PERFORMED; do not print the full bed first.</p><p>Matching slicer project: <a href=\"Creality_Print/EyeTrace_ABS_FitTest_Project_v5.3mf\">EyeTrace_ABS_FitTest_Project_v5.3mf</a>. Settings: 255 C nozzle, 100 C bed, 0.20 mm layers, 3 walls, 100% rectilinear infill, 4 mm brim, supports off; scale 100%, no compensation.</p><p>The parts were rearranged to avoid ring/horn proximity warnings. Coupon geometry and test purposes are retained; all seven are needed.</p><p><b>Prepare:</b> both actual SG90 servos, original star horns and original horn screws/drivers; M3 x 10 screws/nuts for printed interfaces; unpowered camera; smooth gauge pins or camera screws only if they pass freely; calipers. Never force M3 into a servo horn/ear.</p>'+''.join(cards)+'<h2>After printing</h2><ol><li>Cool fully and record corner lift, cracking, layer split, bridge sag and support damage.</li><li>Measure before cleanup; log dimensions, spool batch and settings.</li><li>Test both servos/horns separately; never backdrive SG90 gearing.</li><li>Keep camera unpowered; never press the gauge against lens or PCB parts.</li><li>Coupon PASS does not verify complete motion, camera clearance, load capacity or production readiness.</li></ol><p><a href=\"../DOCUMENTATION/ABS_PRINT_SETTINGS.md\">ABS settings</a> | <a href=\"../DOCUMENTATION/REMAINING_PHYSICAL_VERIFICATION.md\">Remaining verification</a></p></body></html>'
